  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234518/assets/cc3274e21594169662d7b96d0fcadbab1b78a3d944445cc84aad4d37b395bed6.png)\n\nDetermine the volume of the sphere above.",
  "worked_solution": "We can find the volume of a sphere using the formula\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nSubstituting $r=1\\,\\text{in}$ into the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\frac{4}{3}\\pi (1)^{3}=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
